---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const X_HANDLE = '@kenmazaika';
const xUsername = X_HANDLE.slice(1);
const xProfileUrl = `https://x.com/${xUsername}`;
const xFollowUrl = `https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=${xUsername}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Start here: running an AI agent for real work — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="A guided path through choosing, building, and debugging an AI work harness, based on real Hermes and OpenClaw work."
			image="/og/start.png"
			imageAlt={`Run an AI agent for real work — Ken Mazaika, ${X_HANDLE}`}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main" class="start-page">
			<section class="start-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
				<div class="identity">
					<picture>
						<source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/ken/ken-mazaika-256.webp 256w, /images/ken/ken-mazaika-640.webp 640w" sizes="80px" />
						<img src="/images/ken/ken-mazaika-640.jpg" srcset="/images/ken/ken-mazaika-256.jpg 256w, /images/ken/ken-mazaika-640.jpg 640w" sizes="80px" width="80" height="80" alt="Ken Mazaika" />
					</picture>
					<div>
						<p class="identity-cred">Former cofounder of the Firehose project, acquired by Trilogy Education — I developed the curriculum that taught career switchers what they need, and I've taught coding-education workshops for business people at Harvard Business School, RISD, Carnegie Mellon, Babson, and Brown.</p>
						<p class="identity-sub">I'm Ken Mazaika, an engineering manager and operator. I run AI agents on real work, keep the receipts, and write down only what survives outside the demo.</p>
						<a href={xProfileUrl} target="_blank" rel="me noopener">{X_HANDLE} on X</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="eyebrow">A guided reading path</p>
				<h1 id="page-title">Run an AI agent for real work.</h1>
				<a class="follow-primary" href={xFollowUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow {X_HANDLE} on X →</a>
				<p class="dek">AI agents are easy to demo and surprisingly hard to trust. This is my curated path through building and running a dependable AI work harness—based on actual Hermes and OpenClaw work, organized by the question you have now.</p>
				<p class="proof"><strong>One receipt:</strong> 11 models · 5 real tasks · identical prompts · measured costs.</p>
				<form action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/mazaika" method="post" class="receipt-form hero-subscribe">
					<label for="email-hero"><strong>New receipts, weekly-ish.</strong> One email, no newsletter noise.</label>
					<div><input type="email" name="email" id="email-hero" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required /><input type="hidden" name="embed" value="1" /><button type="submit">Subscribe</button></div>
				</form>
				<div class="start-card">
					<div><p class="start-label">New to agents?</p><a href="#what">Start with what a harness does →</a><p>Learn what the layer around a model actually does—and whether your work has the repeatable middle that makes a harness useful.</p></div>
					<div><p class="start-label">Already running one?</p><a href="/blog/best-ai-model-for-agent-work/">Start with the model receipts →</a><p>Eleven models, five real tasks, identical prompts, measured costs, and the raw artifacts.</p></div>
				</div>
				<p class="onramp">Not an engineer, and this is all new? Start with <a href="/blog/what-is-an-ai-harness/">the plain-English definition</a>.</p>
			</section>

			<div class="contents-wrap">
				<nav class="contents" aria-labelledby="contents-title">
					<div class="contents-head"><h2 id="contents-title">On this page</h2><p>Already running agents? Jump to the problem you have now.</p></div>
					<ol>
						<li><a href="#what"><span>01</span>What is a harness?</a></li>
						<li><a href="#choose"><span>02</span>Which setup?</a></li>
						<li><a href="#workflow"><span>03</span>First workflow</a></li>
						<li><a href="#models"><span>04</span>Which models?</a></li>
						<li><a href="#diagnose"><span>05</span>Why is it wrong?</a></li>
					</ol>
				</nav>
			</div>

			<div class="journey">
				<section class="stage" id="what" aria-labelledby="what-title">
					<p class="stage-no">Stage 01</p><h2 id="what-title">What is an AI work harness—and do I need one?</h2>
					<p class="outcome">A harness gives a model tools, memory, instructions, schedules, files, and a place to work. It is useful when a repeated job has a clear middle—not when you only need a one-off answer.</p>
					<a class="featured" href="/blog/what-is-an-ai-harness/"><strong>What Is an AI Work Harness? →</strong><span>Read this for the plain-English definition, the jobs a harness is good at, and the line between automation and judgment.</span></a>
					<p class="support-label">Also useful</p><ul class="support"><li><a href="/blog/my-175-ai-agent-rig/">My $175 AI Agent Rig: What It Really Costs</a></li></ul>
					<p class="bridge">Once the job fits a harness, the next decision is the working environment.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="stage" id="choose" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
					<p class="stage-no">Stage 02</p><h2 id="choose-title">Which setup should I choose?</h2>
					<p class="aside">My short version: OpenClaw is my main tool for assignment fidelity and tighter memory control. I still use Hermes for established workflows and research-oriented work.</p>
					<p class="outcome">Choose the environment whose defaults fit how you work. The differences show up in memory, research, orchestration, and whether the agent follows the assignment you actually gave it.</p>
					<a class="featured" href="/blog/hermes-vs-openclaw/"><strong>Hermes vs. OpenClaw: Why I Moved My Main Workflow →</strong><span>Read my real-work comparison—including where each won and why memory changed my decision.</span></a>
					<p class="support-label">Decision guides</p><ul class="support"><li><a href="/blog/discord-vs-telegram-agentic-work/">Discord vs. Telegram for Agentic Work</a></li></ul>
					<p class="bridge">The platform matters less than the first bounded job you give it.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="stage" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
					<p class="stage-no">Stage 03</p><h2 id="workflow-title">How do I turn a repeated task into a workflow?</h2>
					<p class="outcome">Start with one bounded runbook: a clear trigger, repeatable middle, visible output, and human judgment at the end. Let the agent own coordination without pretending to replace judgment.</p>
					<a class="featured" href="/blog/your-first-useful-hour-with-openclaw/"><strong>Your First Useful Hour With OpenClaw: Build One Automation, End to End →</strong><span>Read this to build your first automation start to finish — pull a source, set the judgment, push it somewhere you can see, wrap it as a skill, and put it on a cron. Every prompt included.</span></a>
					<p class="support-label">Pick the closest shape</p><ul class="support"><li><a href="/blog/capture-workflow/">A Capture Workflow for Work That Contains Your Judgment</a></li><li><a href="/blog/hermes-workflow-apartment-scouting/">Using the Scouting Pattern for Apartment Hunting</a></li><li><a href="/blog/hermes-workflow-i-thought-kanban-was-for-me-to-manage/">I Thought Kanban Was for Me to Manage</a></li><li><a href="/blog/route-the-file-before-you-write-it/">Route the File Before You Write It</a></li><li><a href="/blog/hermes-memory-skills-wiki-learns/">Memory Remembers, Skills Repeat, and a Wiki Learns</a></li></ul>
					<p class="aside">The fastest path is to copy one example's shape — the first-hour walkthrough does exactly that, one automation end to end.</p>
					<p class="bridge">Once the workflow is clear, choose the least expensive model stack that can inspect its own work.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="return-block" aria-labelledby="return-mid-title">
					<p class="eyebrow">Keep the thread</p><h2 id="return-mid-title">New receipts, weekly-ish.</h2><p>One email, no newsletter noise.</p>
					<form action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/mazaika" method="post" class="receipt-form">
						<label for="email-mid">Email address</label><div><input type="email" name="email" id="email-mid" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required /><input type="hidden" name="embed" value="1" /><button type="submit">Subscribe</button></div>
					</form>
					<a class="follow-quiet" href={xFollowUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Or follow {X_HANDLE} on X →</a>
				</section>

				<section class="stage" id="models" aria-labelledby="models-title">
					<p class="stage-no">Stage 04</p><h2 id="models-title">Which models should I use?</h2>
					<p class="aside">For my own work, DeepSeek is the economical daily driver; I use an OpenAI model for a quality anchor or vision.</p>
					<p class="outcome">Use a cheap, capable workhorse for routine steps and a model that can see for visual work and final inspection. You do not need a model zoo.</p>
					<a class="featured" href="/blog/my-default-model-stack-for-ai-agent-work/"><strong>My Default Model Stack for AI Agent Work →</strong><span>See the small stack I actually use for routine work, quality checks, and visual inspection.</span></a>
					<p class="support-label">Build the stack</p><ul class="support"><li><a href="/blog/designing-blind/">Designing Blind</a></li><li><a href="/blog/measuring-ai-impact-on-developer-teams/">Measuring AI's Impact on Developer Teams</a></li></ul>
					<p class="bridge">A weak tool, retrieval failure, or bad handoff can make every model look bad.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="stage" id="diagnose" aria-labelledby="diagnose-title">
					<p class="stage-no">Stage 05</p><h2 id="diagnose-title">What should I check when the agent gets things wrong?</h2>
					<p class="aside">My order: verify tools, inspect evidence, reduce active context, check persistent memory, and only then compare models.</p>
					<p class="outcome">Before switching models, inspect the system around the model: tools, retrieved evidence, active context, and persistent memory.</p>
					<a class="featured" href="/blog/before-you-blame-the-model-audit-your-hermes-setup/"><strong>Before You Blame the Model, Audit Your Hermes Setup →</strong><span>Use a copyable prompt to find missing tools, silent fallbacks, and configuration bottlenecks.</span></a>
					<p class="support-label">Follow the evidence</p><ul class="support"><li><a href="/blog/a-feature-that-makes-your-agent-show-its-receipts/">Does AI Citation Grounding Actually Catch Errors?</a></li><li><a href="/blog/my-agent-kept-writing-the-same-post/">My Agent Kept Writing the Same Post</a></li><li><a href="/blog/i-gave-openclaw-less-memory/">I Gave OpenClaw Less Memory</a></li><li><a href="/blog/more-context-makes-your-agent-dumber/">More Context Makes Your Agent Dumber</a></li></ul>
					<p class="bridge">If the system is still only a pile of good intentions, bring one real runbook and map it with help.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="deep" aria-labelledby="deep-title"><p class="eyebrow">Continue exploring</p><h2 id="deep-title">Already running an agent? Go deeper.</h2><p>These pieces improve leverage rather than merely add complexity.</p><ul><li><a href="/blog/hermes-workflow-question-the-instruction/">Teach Your Agent to Question the Instruction →</a></li><li><a href="/blog/meta-prompting-let-ai-write-your-prompt/">Meta-Prompting: Let the AI Write Your Prompt →</a></li><li><a href="/blog/hermes-workflow-six-bots-one-media-company/">Six Bots, One Media Company →</a></li></ul></section>

				<section class="return-block return-end" id="subscribe-end" aria-labelledby="return-end-title">
					<p class="eyebrow">Come back when the next test is done</p><h2 id="return-end-title">New receipts, weekly-ish.</h2><p>One email, no newsletter noise.</p>
					<form action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/mazaika" method="post" class="receipt-form">
						<label for="email-end">Email address</label><div><input type="email" name="email" id="email-end" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required /><input type="hidden" name="embed" value="1" /><button type="submit">Subscribe</button></div>
					</form>
					<p class="return-links"><a href={xFollowUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow {X_HANDLE} on X</a><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><a href="/blog/">Latest writing</a></p>
					<p class="contact-line">Questions? Reply to any email from me — it comes straight to me.</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	:global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-padding-top: 5.5rem; }
	.start-page { overflow: hidden; }
	.start-hero { max-width: 760px; margin: auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem) 28px 4.5rem; }
	.eyebrow, .stage-no, .start-label, .support-label { color: var(--color-accent); font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600; }
	.eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
	.identity { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.7rem; }
	.identity picture { flex: 0 0 auto; }
	.identity img { display: block; width: 80px; height: 80px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 50%; }
	.identity-cred { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.55; }
	.identity-sub { margin: .4rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.identity a { display: inline-block; margin-top: .35rem; font-size: .77rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.start-hero h1 { max-width: 930px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 6.25vw, 5.75rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.052em; text-wrap: balance; }
	.follow-primary { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: .68rem 1rem; color: #fff; background: var(--color-accent); border-radius: var(--border-radius); font-size: .88rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.onramp { max-width: 760px; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.6; }

	.contact-line { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .84rem; }
	.follow-primary:hover { color: #fff; background: var(--color-accent-hover); }
	.dek { max-width: 700px; margin: 1.6rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.65vw, 1.22rem); line-height: 1.65; }
	.proof { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding-left: .9rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.55; }
	.receipt-form { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
	.receipt-form label { display: block; margin-bottom: .45rem; font-size: .82rem; }
	.receipt-form > div { display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
	.receipt-form input[type='email'] { flex: 1; min-width: 0; padding: .72rem .8rem; color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--border-radius); font: inherit; font-size: .88rem; }
	.receipt-form input[type='email']:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
	.receipt-form button { padding: .72rem .95rem; color: #fff; background: var(--color-accent); border: 0; border-radius: var(--border-radius); font: inherit; font-size: .86rem; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
	.hero-subscribe { max-width: 560px; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.hero-subscribe button { color: var(--color-accent); background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); }
	.hero-subscribe button:hover { color: #fff; background: var(--color-accent); }
	.start-card { max-width: 760px; margin-top: 2.4rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; background: var(--color-bg-card); border-top: 2px solid var(--color-accent); box-shadow: 0 12px 35px rgba(38,28,18,.06); }
	.start-card > div { padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
	.start-card > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.start-label { margin: 0 0 .35rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.start-card a { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 600; }
	.start-card div > p:last-child { margin: .45rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.55; }
	.contents-wrap { background: var(--color-bg-secondary); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.contents { max-width: 1120px; margin: auto; padding: 2rem 28px; }
	.contents-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1.15rem; }
	.contents h2 { margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; }
	.contents-head p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .82rem; }
	.contents ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
	.contents li { min-width: 0; border-left: 1px solid #d8d1c7; padding: .2rem 1rem .3rem; }
	.contents li:first-child { border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); }
	.contents a { display: block; color: var(--color-text); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: .98rem; line-height: 1.25; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
	.contents a span { display: block; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: .68rem; margin-bottom: .3rem; }
	.journey { max-width: 760px; margin: auto; padding: 2rem 28px 6rem; }
	.stage { padding: 5.4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: 74px; }
	.stage-no { margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
	.stage h2 { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 3.8vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.035em; text-wrap: balance; }
	.outcome { margin: .1rem 0 1.6rem; font-size: 1.01rem; line-height: 1.7; }
	.featured { display: block; padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem; background: var(--color-bg-card); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text); }
	.featured strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.32rem; line-height: 1.25; }
	.featured span { display: block; margin-top: .45rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.55; }
	.support-label { margin: 1.65rem 0 .55rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.support { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
	.support li { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: .7rem 0; }
	.support a { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.45; font-weight: 500; }
	.aside { margin: 1.2rem 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: .96rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	.bridge { margin: 1.8rem 0 -2.7rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-style: italic; font-size: 1rem; }
	.deep { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.deep h2 { padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: 2.35rem; line-height: 1.08; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
	.deep > p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.deep ul { list-style: none; margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
	.deep li { padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.deep li a { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.return-block { margin: 0; padding: 3rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.return-block h2 { margin: 0 0 .4rem; padding: 0; border: 0; font-size: 1.8rem; }
	.return-block > p:not(.eyebrow, .return-links) { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.follow-quiet { display: inline-block; margin-top: .9rem; font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 600; }
	.return-end { margin-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 0; }
	.return-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .55rem; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; font-size: .84rem; }
	@media (max-width: 900px) { .contents ol { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); row-gap: 1.1rem; } .contents li:nth-child(3), .contents li:nth-child(5) { border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); } }
	@media (max-width: 680px) { .start-hero { padding: 1.6rem 20px 3rem; } .identity { gap: .8rem; margin-bottom: 1.15rem; } .identity img { width: 72px; height: 72px; } .identity-cred { font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.45; } .identity-sub { font-size: .68rem; line-height: 1.35; } .identity a { font-size: .7rem; } .start-hero .eyebrow { margin-bottom: .65rem; } .start-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 9vw, 3rem); line-height: 1; } .follow-primary { margin-top: .85rem; padding: .58rem .8rem; font-size: .8rem; } .dek { font-size: 1rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; } .start-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-top: 2rem; } .start-card > div { padding: 1.2rem; } .start-card > div + div { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); } .start-card a { font-size: 1.25rem; } .contents { padding: 1.6rem 20px; } .contents-head { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; } .contents-head p { margin-top: .35rem; } .contents ol { gap: .75rem 0; } .contents li { padding: .2rem .8rem; } .journey { padding: 0 20px 4rem; } .stage { padding: 4rem 0; } .stage h2 { font-size: 2.05rem; } .outcome { font-size: .96rem; } .featured { padding: 1.15rem; width: 100%; } .featured strong { font-size: 1.23rem; } .bridge { margin-bottom: -2rem; } .deep { padding-top: 4rem; } .deep h2 { font-size: 2rem; } }
	@media (max-width: 520px) { .receipt-form > div { flex-direction: column; } .receipt-form button { width: 100%; } }
	@media (max-width: 360px) { .start-hero, .contents, .journey { padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; } .start-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 9vw, 3rem); } .identity img { width: 72px; height: 72px; } .contents ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .contents li, .contents li:nth-child(3), .contents li:nth-child(5) { border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); } }
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { :global(html) { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
</style>
